[{'CONTRACT_AWARD_ID': 'W911W6-22-P-0005', 'CONTRACT_SOLICITATION_ID': 'MZ-JandA22-1144', 'AWARD_NAME': 'Fortus 450MC Gen II System', 'AWARD_DESCRIPTION': "Army Contract Command - Redstone Arsenal, Technology Development Directorate - Aviation, located in Fort Eustis, Virginia, intends to solicit orally and award a Firm Fixed Price purchase order on a sole source basis to TriMech Solutions, LLC, located at 4991 Lake Brook Dr Ste 300, Glen Allen, VA 23060-9293,  for a Stratasys 450 MC 3-D Printer purchase.  The anticipated award date is 31 May 2022.  This notice of intent is not a request for competitive quotes. All responsible sources may submit a bid, proposal or quotation, which shall be considered by the agency; however, a determination by the Government not to compete this proposed purchase order based upon responses to this notice is solely within the discretion of the Government. The Government intends to solicit and negotiate with only one source under the authority of FAR 13.106(b)(1) Soliciting from a Single Source. A justification to not compete this acquisition has been properly executed and is included with this notice. The justification addresses the requirements of FAR 5.207(c)(15), reason for lack of competition. The NAICS Code for this requirement is 333249 and the associated size standard is 500.  The PSC is 3695.  If your firm possesses the ability to meet this requirement, then you must respond by demonstrating your firm's technical capability to meet these requirements no later than 12:00 Noon EST on 31 May 2022 to Deanna Van Cleaf, email deanna.c.vancleaf.civ@army.mil and Bethany Rosser, email bethany.r.rosser.civ.army.mil.   Purchase Order was awarded on a sole source basis.", 'AWARD_AMOUNT': 107975.0, 'AWARD_DATE': '2022-05-31', 'RECIPIENT': 'Trimech Solutions, Llc Va  Usa', 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_ID': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_NAME': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_TITLE': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_EMAIL': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_PHONE': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_FAX': None}, {'CONTRACT_AWARD_ID': 'W912DW-05-D-1027 TO 2164', 'CONTRACT_SOLICITATION_ID': 'W912DW05D1027TBD', 'AWARD_NAME': 'RECOVERY--Y--PROJECT NUMBER 32213, Flagship Construct Showers in Latrine Areas, 3-2 SBCT, 3651, BN Headquarters, PROJECT NUMBER 33051, Flagship Construct Showers in Latrine Areas, 3-2 SBCT, 3734, BN Headquarters', 'AWARD_DESCRIPTION': 'RECOVERY PER FAR 5.7 THIS NOTICE IS PROVIDED FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES ONLY; THEREFORE FAR 5.203 DOES NOT APPLY. THIS OPPORTUNITY IS AVAILABLE ONLY TO THE CONTRACTOR UNDER THE CURRENT CONTRACT NUMBER: Centennial Contractors Enterprises, Inc, W912DW-05-D-1027. Program Name: Job Order Contract in Support of Fort Lewis Public Works and Other Customers Supported by Seattle District Corps of Engineers RECOVERY -- PROJECT NUMBER 32213, Flagship Construct Showers in Latrine Areas, 3-2 SBCT, 3651 BN Headquarters and RECOVERY -- PROJECT NUMBER 33051, Flagship Construct Showers in Latrine Areas, 3-2 SBCT, 3734 BN Headquarters This is an order under an existing contract that was awarded using competitive procedures. Under this Task Order (for project number 32213), the contractor shall renovate Room 123 (mens restroom) and 126 (womens restroom), and the latrine area room C30 (womens restroom) and C27 (mens restroom), at Building 3651, Fort Lewis, Washington. The contractor shall construct one shower stall in the womens restroom (room 126) and three shower stalls in the mens restroom (room 123). The project scope consists of demolishing southern and western walls of Room 124 and demolishing two lavatories mounted on northern walls of the mens restroom. Any fire alarms, electrical and communication devices and their respective conduits will also need to be demolished. New installation includes: installing fiberglass shower stalls; shower heads; shower valves for each stall; new, recessed, wet location rated fixture above each shower stall; appropriately sized exhaust register above the new shower stall in room 126. A plumbing layout will need to be developed for the new shower stalls. The water heating system will need to be upgraded to support the maximum demand for hot water in building 3651. Restore all areas affected by the construction of the new shower stalls. This work will take place at building 3651, Fort Lewis, Washington. Under this Task Order (for project number 33051), the contractor shall renovate Room C27 (mens restroom) and C30 (womens restroom), at Building 3734, Fort Lewis, Washington. The contractor shall construct one shower stall in the womens restroom (room C30) by taking the area of the existing janitors closet (room C29) and three shower stalls in the mens restroom (room C27). The project scope consists of demolishing ceilings above the shower room located in room C27; demolishing lighting fixtures, shower head, shower faucet and floor drain in the existing shower room. Demolish existing western wall portions of the southern wall, door and all electrical devices/appurtenances in Room C29. New installation includes: shower head; shower valve; soap holder; towel hook and shower curtain for each of the stalls; and two new, surface mount, wet location rated fixture above the three shower stalls. A plumbing layout will need to be developed for the new shower stalls. The water heating system will need to be upgraded to support the maximum demand for hot water in building 3734. Restore all areas affected by the construction of the new shower stalls. This work will take place at building 3734, Fort Lewis, Washington. Magnitude of Construction for both projects is $25K - $100K and the completion period is estimated at 120 calendar days. The NAICS code for this project is 236220. One or more of the items under this acquisition is subject to the World Trade Organization Government Procurement Agreement and Free Trade Agreements. RECOVERY - PER FAR 5.7 THIS NOTICE IS PROVIDED FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES ONLY; THEREFORE FAR 5.203 DOES NOT APPLY. THIS OPPORTUNITY WAS AVAILABLE ONLY TO CONTRACTOR(S) UNDER THE CURRENT CONTRACT NUMBER(S): Centennial Contractors Enterprises, W912DW-05-D-1027 TO 2164 This award notice is for a task order that was issued under an existing Job Order Contract (JOC) Indefinite-Delivery Type Contract which was awarded using competitive procedures. The projects provide for renovations to construct showers in latrine areas at 3651 and 3734 BN Headquarters located on Ft. Lewis, Washington. The NAICS code for this requirement is 236220.', 'AWARD_AMOUNT': 113723.33, 'AWARD_DATE': '2010-03-05', 'RECIPIENT': 'Centennial Contractors Enterprises, Inc.  11111 Sunset Hills Rd, Ste 350 Reston, Va', 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_ID': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_NAME': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_TITLE': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_EMAIL': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_PHONE': None, 'PRIMARY_AWARDER_CONTACT_FAX': None}, {'CONTRACT_AWARD_ID': 'N00164-05-D-6412', 'CONTRACT_SOLICITATION_ID': 'N0016405R6412', 'AWARD_NAME': '58--Inertial Navigation Units', 'AWARD_DESCRIPTION': 'N00164-05-R-6412 INERTIAL NAVIGATION UNITS -FSG 58 - NAICS 334511 Issue Date 24 May 2005 - Closing Date 07 June 2005 \x96 2:00 PM EST This synopsis is being posted to both the Federal Business Opportunities (FBO) page located at http://www.eps.gov and the Navy Electronic Commerce on Line (NECO) site located at http://www.neco.navy.mil. While it is understood that FBO is the single point of entry for posting of synopsis and solicitations to the Internet, NECO is the alternative in case FBO is unavailable. Please feel free to use either site to access information posted by NSWC Crane. This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial items prepared in accordance with the format in FAR 12.6, as supplemented with additional information included in this notice. This announcement constitutes the only solicitation; proposals are being requested and a written solicitation will not be issued. Solicitation Number N00164-05-R-6412 is hereby issued as a Request for Proposal (RFP). Incorporated provisions and clauses are those in effect through Federal Acquisition Circular 2001-27 as well as DCN 20050222. The North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) Code for this procurement is 334511 and the size standard is 750 employees. This procurement will utilize full & open competition. This requirement is for the following: CLIN 0001 \x96 Base INU without integrated GPS (IAW attached salient characteristics), CLIN 0002 \x96 Base INU with integrated GPS (IAW attached salient characteristics), CLIN 0003 \x96 *Improved Azimuth Performance INU without integrated GPS (IAW attached salient characteristics), CLIN 0004 \x96 *Improved Azimuth Performance INU with integrated GPS (IAW attached salient characteristics). *Note: Improved azimuth means that the maximum azimuth error is 2 mils instead of 5 mils. The minimum and maximum quantities for CLIN 0001 & CLIN 0002 combined are min = 1 each, max = 50 each. The minimum and maximum quantities for CLIN 0003 & CLIN 0004 combined are min = 0 each, max = 50 each. Offerors are required to propose any applicable quantity price breaks. Delivery is required F.O.B. destination (NSWC Crane, 47522). The Government required delivery date (RDD) for the first INU is 1 Aug 2005. For the remainder of the IDIQ contract, delivery for mate! rials shall be either 45 days after order (for small quantities of less than or equal to 5 units) or 180 days after order (for large quantities of greater than 5 units). Final inspection & acceptance will occur at NSWC Crane. Selection for award will be based on past performance and price. The offeror shall demonstrate past performance through completion of the "Contractor Performance Data Sheet (Found at www.crane.navy.mil/supply/homepage.htm)". The Contractor Performance Data Sheet shall be completed in its entirety. Additionally, offerors are urged to submit brief and concise responses, within the confines of the s
