[{'TRADE_EVENT_ID': 'ITA-aW5ldmVudC04MDkyNA', 'TRADE_EVENT_NAME': 'U.S. Commercial Service Meetings at NAFSA 2024', 'START_DATE': '2024-05-28', 'END_DATE': '2024-05-31', 'RELEVANT_INDUSTRIES': '[\n  "Education"\n]', 'TRADE_EVENT_TYPE': 'In-Person', 'TRADE_EVENT_URL': 'https://www.trade.gov/attend-event', 'TRADE_EVENT_DESCRIPTION': '<p style="margin:0in;font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;color:#4a4a4a;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.01rem;background-color:#ffffff;"><span style="font-size:14pt;">The U.S. Commercial Service’s Global Education Team is offering onsite matchmaking at NAFSA 2024 from May 28 to May 31 in New Orleans, LA:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;color:#4a4a4a;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.01rem;background-color:#ffffff;"><span style="font-size:14pt;">For overseas agents, counselors, and university partners, you have the opportunity to schedule meetings with U.S. Study State Consortia from 12 States.\xa0</span></li>\n<li style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;color:#4a4a4a;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.01rem;background-color:#ffffff;"><span style="font-size:14pt;">For U.S. Education Institutions and Study State Consortia, you have the opportunity to schedule one-on-one meetings with the U.S. Commercial Service (CS) representatives from several overseas markets. \xa0These CS Education Specialists are able to advise U.S. institutions on market selection, education policy, landscape, and understanding foreign students\' preferences.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style="margin:0in;font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;color:#4a4a4a;font-family:Calibri, sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.01rem;background-color:#ffffff;"><span style="font-size:14pt;"><span style="letter-spacing:0.01rem;">All the meetings will take place at the\xa0</span><span style="letter-spacing:0.01rem;font-weight:bolder;">USA: A Study Destination Pavilion (Booth P1301).</span></span></p>', 'REGISTRATION_TYPE': None, 'REGISTRATION_URL': 'https://events.trade.gov/en/TradeGov/USCommercialServiceMeetingsatNAFSA2024/index.php', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_COUNTRY': 'country/USA', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_STATE': 'geoId/22', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_NAME': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_STREET': 'New Orleans Ernest N. Morial Convention Center', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_CITY': 'Orleans Parish', 'SECONDARY_VENUE': None, 'TERTIARY_VENUE': None, 'CONTACTS': '[{"email":"alexandra.natale@trade.gov","name":null,"person_title":null,"phone":null,"post":null}]'}, {'TRADE_EVENT_ID': 'ITA-aW5ldmVudC04MjkxNw', 'TRADE_EVENT_NAME': 'Canadian Emergency Preparedness and Climate Adaptation Convention (CEPCA) 2024', 'START_DATE': '2024-09-24', 'END_DATE': '2024-09-26', 'RELEVANT_INDUSTRIES': '[\n  "Fire Safety and Rescue Equipment",\n  "Public Safety",\n  "Safety and Protection",\n  "Safety and Security",\n  "Security and Safety Equipment"\n]', 'TRADE_EVENT_TYPE': 'In-Person', 'TRADE_EVENT_URL': 'https://www.trade.gov/attend-event', 'TRADE_EVENT_DESCRIPTION': '<div>CEPCA – Canadian Emergency Preparedness and Climate Adaptation was established as a national event to bring together communities, stakeholders, and individuals responsible for managing, responding to, and planning for emergencies and natural disasters across Canada. For the 2024 convention, the key focus is on how Canada can better connect isolated supply chains, community strategies, policies, and access to current information amidst our vast geography and diverse threats.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>At CEPCA, we recognize the importance of fostering collaboration and breaking down silos in both emergency management and climate adaptation to enhance public safety. This event is not only an opportunity for buyers to explore innovative solutions but also a platform for exhibitors to showcase cutting-edge products and services. By bringing together leaders and innovators from across the country, we aim to address today’s pressing issues while preparing for tomorrow’s challenges. Join us in Ottawa from September 24–26, 2024, to contribute to a more unified and coordinated approach to emergency response by connecting municipal, provincial, and federal stakeholders—all under one roof.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>To register as an exhibitor or attendee, please visit: https://www.emergencyexpo.com/register/</div>', 'REGISTRATION_TYPE': None, 'REGISTRATION_URL': 'https://events.trade.gov/en/TradeGov/CanadianEmergencyPreparednessandClimateAdaptationC/index.php', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_COUNTRY': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_STATE': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_NAME': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_STREET': '55 Colonel By Drive', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_CITY': 'Ottawa', 'SECONDARY_VENUE': None, 'TERTIARY_VENUE': None, 'CONTACTS': '[]'}, {'TRADE_EVENT_ID': 'ITA-aW5ldmVudC04MTY0Mw', 'TRADE_EVENT_NAME': 'Cyber Opportunities in the Middle East', 'START_DATE': '2024-05-15', 'END_DATE': '2024-05-15', 'RELEVANT_INDUSTRIES': '[\n  "Computer Systems",\n  "Cybersecurity",\n  "Information Services",\n  "Information Technology Services",\n  "Information and Communications Technology",\n  "Security Services",\n  "Security Technology",\n  "Software"\n]', 'TRADE_EVENT_TYPE': 'Virtual / Online', 'TRADE_EVENT_URL': 'https://www.trade.gov/attend-event', 'TRADE_EVENT_DESCRIPTION': '<span style="color:#34495e;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><span style="background:#fcfcfc;">Join the U.S. Commercial Service for a webinar detailing the cybersecurity sectors in four Middle Eastern markets. Hear from cybersecurity experts about everything from regional trends to country specific regulations to market entry strategies.\xa0<br /><br />Register now to learn about opportunities for U.S. cybersecurity companies in <b>Bahrain, Jordan, Kuwait and Qatar!\xa0</b><br /><br /><span style="font-size:18pt;"><i><b>Discussion Topics:</b></i><br /></span>Working with the public and private sectors, what are the local business customs? Which sectors are looking to increase their cybersecurity (Critical Infrastructure, Healthcare, Finance, Oil & Gas, etc.)?<br />Have there been any major cyber-attacks in the market?<br />What are the local cybersecurity industry events?<br />And much more....<br /><br /><span style="font-size:18pt;"><b><i>Agenda</i>:</b></span><br />11:00am: Introductions & Opening Remarks\xa0<br />11:05am: <b>Bahrain </b>Market Overview\xa0<br />11:15am: <b>Jordan </b>Market Overview <br />11:25am: <b>Kuwait </b>Market Overview<br />11:35am <b>Qatar </b>Market Overview\xa0<br />11:45pm Q&A<br /><br /><span style="font-size:18pt;"><b><i>Speakers</i>:</b></span><br /></span><span style="background:#fcfcfc;"><b>Imane Alalaiwat,</b> Commercial Specialist, U.S. Embassy Manama\xa0</span></span>\n<div>\n<div><span style="color:#34495e;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><b>Lubna Abdelhadi, </b>Commercial Specialist, U.S. Embassy Amman</span><br /><span style="color:#34495e;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><b>Rasha Al-Muhtaseb,</b> Commercial Specialist, U.S Embassy Kuwait City</span></div>\n<div>\n<div><span style="color:#34495e;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><b>Juan Catril, </b>Commercial Advisor, U.S. Embassy Doha<br /><br /><i><b><span style="font-size:18pt;">Logistics:</span></b></i><br /><span style="background-color:#fcfcfc;">Cost: $25</span><br /><span style="background-color:#fcfcfc;">Location: Virtual\xa0</span><br /><span style="background-color:#fcfcfc;">Time: May 15th, 2024 at 11:00amEST/8:00am PT</span><br /></span></div>\n</div>\n<div></div>\n</div>', 'REGISTRATION_TYPE': None, 'REGISTRATION_URL': 'https://events.trade.gov/en/TradeGov/CyberOpportunitiesintheMiddleEast-9884-1711648972/index.php', 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_COUNTRY': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_GEO_ID_STATE': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_NAME': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_STREET': None, 'PRIMARY_VENUE_CITY': None, 'SECONDARY_VENUE': None, 'TERTIARY_VENUE': None, 'CONTACTS': '[{"email":"samantha.feder@trade.gov","name":null,"person_title":null,"phone":null,"post":null}]'}, {'TRADE_EVENT_ID': 'ITA-aW5ldmVudC04MDMyMw', 'TRADE_EVENT_NAME': 'SelectUSA Mexico Conference', 'START_DATE': '2024-03-12', 'END_DATE': '2024-03-14', 'RELEVANT_INDUSTRIES': '[\n  "3D Printing",\n  "Accommodations",\n  "Accounting Services",\n  "Adhesives and Sealants",\n  "Adult Education and Training",\n  "Advertising Services",\n  "Agricultural Biotechnology",\n  "Agricultural Chemicals",\n  "Agricultural Commodities",\n  "Agricultural Equipment and Machinery",\n  "Air Pollution Control",\n  "Air Transportation",\n  "Apparel",\n  "Armored Vehicles",\n  "Artificial Intelligence",\n  "Artwork",\n  "Asset Management",\n  "Audio-Visual Equipment",\n  "Automotive Parts",\n  "Automotive Retailers",\n  "Autotech",\n  "Aviation",\n  "Baby Food",\n  "Bakeries",\n  "Banking",\n  "Beverages",\n  "Biopharmaceuticals",\n  "Biopharmaceuticals: Equipment and Manufacturing",\n  "Boating",\n  "Brand Merchandise Licensing",\n  "Building Products",\n  "Business Associations",\n  "Business Equipment",\n  "Catalog and Mail Order",\n  "Ceramics",\n  "Chambers of Commerce",\n  "Chemical Production Machinery",\n  "Civil Nuclear Power",\n  "Cloud Computing",\n  "Coal",\n  "Coatings",\n  "Composites",\n  "Computer Hardware",\n  "Computer Systems",\n  "Computer-Aided Technologies",\n  "Condiments and Seasonings",\n  "Confectionary Products",\n  "Construction Equipment and Machinery",\n  "Consumer Electronics",\n  "Convenience Stores",\n  "Corporate Traini"\n]', 'TRADE_EVENT_TYPE': 'In-Person', 'TRADE_EVENT_URL': 'https://www.trade.gov/attend-event', 'TRADE_EVENT_DESCRIPTION': "<h2>SelectUSA Mexico Conference\xa0</h2>\n<h3>The SelectUSA Mexico Conference is set to become a must-attend event for U.S. economic developers seeking to attract Mexican investments.</h3>\n<h3>The SelectUSA Mexico Conference will enable U.S. state, local, and regional economic development organizations (EDOs) to directly showcase their offerings to qualified Mexican investors and prospects. Conversely, it equips Mexican investors and startups 
